## Summary

**Goal.** Finish moving the client pages under `web/` onto the server's generated link columns (follow-up to 3427f8b, which made `href` a generated column), so that link rules live only on the server and the client builds no page addresses.

**Design, settled with ian in several rounds:**
- Generated columns, each returned only when a query names it (no forced-on columns):
  - `path`: the in-app relative address. `/p/<slug, else id>` for a PERSON, `/g/<slug, else id>` for a GROUP, the wiki path for a wiki DOCUMENT.
  - Per-app absolute hrefs, blank when the row isn't that app's kind of thing: `who_href` (person, family, classroom, grade), `loop_href` (group, event, party, activity), `when_href` (event, party or activity with a start), `team_href` (activity), `celebrate_href` (party).
  - `href` stays the main page for Ask, MCP and mail.
- Person links use the slug, not the ID; ian chose this, and it matches `PERSON.slug`'s own description.
- Every app routes `/g/<key>` to its own view of the group. Who? picks the family, classroom, grade or list page by kind (`kindAt` in `web/who/state.js`). Who? routes `/p/<key>` for people. The `/p/` clash with Celebrate's old prefix and the wiki's `/p/` was accepted, since they are on different hosts.
- Old prefixes (Who?'s `/people/`, `/families/`, `/classrooms/`, `/grades/`, `/groups/`; Loop's `/groups/`; When's `/e/`, `/events/`; Team's `/v/`, `/activities/`; Celebrate's `/p/`, `/parties/`) get a 301 to the same rest under the new prefix. This runs before sign-in, so share previews keep working, and after Team's and Celebrate's REDIRECT-table wraps, because production REDIRECT rows name old paths. It is the `Moved` field on each app in `internal/app/wiring.go`.
- Links within an app use `path`. Links across apps use the app's href. `link()` in `web/public/common/elements.js` marks only relative hrefs for the router, which replaced `railLink`'s special case.
- Writes return only IDs. The two places that need a new row's address right after writing it query `path` afterwards rather than adding columns to the write API (ian's choice): Who?'s tag duplicate/create and When's slug rename.
- Links into the current app's own view of a group stay app routes: Loop's and Who?'s sidebar lists and When's `/g/` page for parties. That was ian's call.

**What was built.** The server generates and documents the columns and serves the read grants and routes. Previews, invites and feeds use `path`. On the client, `personLink`, `familyLink`, `classroomPath`, `gradePath`, `groupPathOf`, `eventPath`, `linkURL`, `profileLink` and `whoLink` were deleted, along with the hand-built `/p/`, `/v/` and `/e/` addresses in Home, alerts, calendar, Celebrate, Team, Loop and Who?. The user menu's profile link comes from `who_href` through `data.js`'s `me()`. The unused `rulesEditor` in `web/common/rules.js` was deleted. Docs were updated (`docs/dev.md` "Where its page is", plus the app docs). Tests cover the columns, the redirects (signed out, in order with REDIRECT rows) and the previews.

**Left out or left alone.**
- Wiki URLs are unchanged. ian: "leave wiki however it is for urls"; a `/d/` scheme for documents was discussed and deferred. A `path` column was added to wiki documents only so the wiki's own links read it.
- The editors' typed-slug address previews still show a `/g/<typed>` prefix, since no row exists yet.
- Staff Birthdays' `/staff/<handle>` pages are an in-app view and were left as is.
- No production page check was possible: production runs the old code, so only data was read from it. Pages were checked on sample data with `tools/console` and `tools/screenshot`.

