### Who?'s person links use the person's slug (`/people/ian.gulliver`), but the server's generated `href` uses their ID (`/people/perWPWxQkmB98q`). Which address should a person's page have, everywhere?

**Background.** The task is to make every client page under `web/` link people, groups and documents through the generated `href` column (added in 3427f8b, computed in `internal/db/link.go`) and delete the client's own link-building code. For people the two rules disagree today:

- **Client** (`personLink` in `web/who/people.js`, also `web/common/directory.js` `profileLink`, `whoLink` in `web/common/appswitch.js`): `/people/<slug>`, falling back to the ID. `PERSON.slug` is the part of a person's primary email before the @, written by the import; its schema description says it is "their short name in Who?'s addresses (/people/<slug>)". Guests have none.
- **Server** (`personHref`): always `https://who.<domain>/people/<id>`. This is what Ask, MCP, search and mail already link to.

Who? opens a person page at either form (`personByKey` takes a slug or an ID), so both work; the question is only which one people see and share.

**Real row (production, you):** `PERSON perWPWxQkmB98q`, `name_show` Ian Gulliver, `slug` ian.gulliver, `href` https://who.heliosian.com/people/perWPWxQkmB98q

| | Your card in Who?'s directory links to | Ask / MCP / mail link to |
