| Client switches to today's `href` | `who.heliosian.com/people/perWPWxQkmB98q` | `who.heliosian.com/people/perWPWxQkmB98q` |
| `personHref` uses the slug, client uses `href` | `who.heliosian.com/people/ian.gulliver` | `who.heliosian.com/people/ian.gulliver` |

- (*) Server uses the slug
  Change `personHref` to `/people/<slug>`, else the ID (a guest), matching the column's own description and the addresses Who? shows today. Every client link then uses `href`. Ask/MCP/mail links change from the ID form to the slug form; old ID links still open.
- ( ) Keep the ID
  Leave `personHref` as it is; Who?'s links change from `/people/ian.gulliver` to `/people/perWPWxQkmB98q`. The `PERSON.slug` description would be corrected to say it is only accepted, not linked.

